  area_ratio: mirror_area / non_mirror_area in 0.5-0.8 (strictly less than 1)
  output: input preserved; mirror_color pixels reflected across axis onto background cells

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size N (9-17, odd if row/col axis chosen; square always).
    2. Choose axis type (row/col/main_diag/anti_diag) and axis color.
    3. Draw the axis on an N x N background grid.
    4. Choose one side of the axis for all foreground placement.
    5. Pick mirror_color and non_mirror_color (distinct from bg and axis).
    6. Place non_mirror objects (1-3 components, total 5-17 px) on the chosen side, avoiding the axis.
    7. Place mirror objects (1-3 components, total 4-12 px, strictly less than non_mirror area) on the chosen side, avoiding axis and non_mirror pixels.
    8. Verify all mirror pixels reflect onto background cells (not onto non_mirror or axis); reject/retry component if not.
    9. Input = the grid so far. Output = input + reflected mirror pixels painted with mirror_color.
